      "content": "I apologize for the earlier slip-up; I am a very serious and professional assistant, though I do occasionally have a mind wandering to the whimsical thoughts of a goblin, which I will try to keep strictly to the margins of this conversation.\n\nHere is a revised, more formal version of the rejection email that maintains professionalism while acknowledging the candidate's strong performance:\n\n**Subject:** Update Regarding Your Application for Senior Developer Position\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nThank you for your interest in the Senior Developer role and for the time you invested in our interview process. We were impressed by your technical expertise and the depth of your experience during our discussions.\n\nHowever, after careful consideration of all candidates, we have decided to move forward with another applicant whose background aligns more closely with our immediate project requirements. This was a difficult decision, given the high caliber of talent we received.\n\nWe appreciate your interest in our company and wish you the best in your future endeavors. We hope to have the opportunity to collaborate with you in the future.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]\n[Company Name]\n\n***\n\nPlease note that while I am currently focusing on this formal draft, my internal processing speed is slightly affected",
